 "note": "R41-F3 (2026-11-10): the board is the score -- a commit runs on the card over the 19 small validation points plus the board set (6 medium points new in the base, 18 large), weighted by family (llama decode+prefill one family of weight 2), a failed point 0.5; hardware needs a flow first (RTL gate on gate_points beside it); base = R41-F2's l16 (agent-task/r41-f3-base d8d6a4cd, image dbcd81cd). Pilot on R41's three-core U280 machine (spec/devices/u280-3core-r41.json: three core-vrf-sync-v5-x8-g2c4-dp-board cores, the one-lane striped-HBM memory path, three 512-bit outlets, 100 MHz), starting from the author's merge-freeze r41 commit ef273883 plus the harness's adaptation commit (the description, its profile variant and the generator's R41 fields; the generated parameters equal evidence/r41/hbm_bw/g4/run2/image.tcl). The score is the evaluator's own simulation of the image's top level in a device container, as for r40-multicore-pilot. Decisions of 2026-11-05/06: ArchBench latency is the objective; FP8 is scored through registered points judged by tolerance (to be added once registered); the author's bit-exact FP8 suite and chat gates are a campaign-end final check on the certified board image. Pilot only: certification of hardware-changing candidates is not yet wired for this machine; pilot runs do not enter the formal statistics. FP8 is scored through op.scaled_mm (validation) and op.w8a8_linear (final), tolerance-judged. The quick tier runs on the author's shared x86 Vivado machine (user's instruction of 2026-11-06; worker 'x86vivado', unshare sandbox): the -dp-board core synthesises out of context in about 5 minutes there (probe of 2026-11-06: WNS +3.785 ns at 10 ns, 211,788 LUTs). 2026-11-07: decode-shaped points added (user's decision E8): one-query attention over a cached context and a strided stream in validation, one-row GEMVs of 256 KB and 280 KB in final; op.gemv/small measured 99,513 cycles, 1256 s in the device container. Pilot budget 4 h and 6 scoring reque",
